From cb35b084c24ae5f9c1d0dcf847fb619197401cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 10:51:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0077 -- S3-2 Stage 1: VRAM-resident always-VRAM
 page-flip (S3 ViRGE/DX)

Retargets the wave-50 VRAM-resident page-flip (patch 0061, Cirrus 5434) to
the S3 ViRGE/DX per the S3-2 de-risk verdict (docs/internal/S3-2-FINAL-
VERDICT.md = GREEN_VRAM_RESIDENT_WINS): the S3 writes VRAM at ~60 MB/s and
dropping the present-copy nets a MEASURED -2.89 ms/frame (FRAME_VRAM 8.18 <
FRAME_SYS 11.06), where the same mechanism LOST on the slow-VRAM Cirrus.

Stage 1 = the SIMPLEST correct model: ZERO engine change. When engaged, the
engine composites the full frame straight into an off-screen VRAM page and
the present becomes a display-start page-flip with no copy:

  - CreateWindowFramebuffer is unchanged (returns the sysmem surface), so
    window creation stays byte-identical.
  - SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull, when engaged, auto-detects whether the
    source pixels are already the hidden VRAM page (steady state -> SKIP the
    copy = the dropped present-copy win) or a sysmem buffer (first frame /
    sysmem-composited frame -> copy sysmem to the hidden page), then flips
    the hidden page to visible via VBE 0x4F07 and repoints
    window->surface->pixels at the new hidden page. The engine's existing
    unconditional per-flip SDL_GetWindowSurface re-query then composites the
    next frame straight into VRAM -- no engine code change. The surface-
    pixels repoint mirrors the proven slow-path LFB page-flip pattern
    (DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer sets dst->pixels to the new back page).

Approved properties:
  - Chip gate: S3 ViRGE/DX (unlock CR38=0x48/CR39=0xA5, read device-ID
    CR2D/CR2E, gate strict 0x8A01), decoupled from the Cirrus gate /
    SDL_HINT_DOS_CIRRUS_BLT.
  - Flip via chip-agnostic VBE 0x4F07 (scanline = offset/pitch), replacing
    the Cirrus-specific direct-CRTC programming.
  - HANG-SAFE engage: at first engage, self-verify 0x4F07 via GET / SET(1-
    scanline test) / GET-readback / restore, all BX=0x0000 (set immediately,
    NO BIOS retrace-wait so the call cannot spin on a missing retrace).
    AX!=0x004F or a readback mismatch DISABLES the lever -> copy-present
    fallback. Per-flip uses 0x4F07 BX=0x0000 then a BOUNDED vblank wait
    AFTER the program (the stock WaitForVBlank is unbounded). Waiting after
    fixes the wave-50 flicker and the bound prevents a HW-IO hang
    (dosbox_not_proxy: a broken flip can hard-freeze g2k).
  - Engaged only on the LFB path (use_dosmemput == false; the banked path
    has no nearptr the engine could composite into) and pitches_match (so
    the surface pitch never changes under the engine).

Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOS_VRAM_RESIDENT stays strict-"1" default-OFF; the
OFF path falls through to the legacy copy-present, byte-identical to pre-0061.
Alpha/RMW composites land in VRAM in this always-VRAM model (slow-but-correct
under the default-OFF killswitch; the KPI Mimiga scene is write-only so it is
not exercised there -- per-frame alpha-vs-writeonly routing is deferred to
Stage 1.5). Removed the dead Cirrus CRTC[0x14]/[0x17]/SR[0x07] sanity check +
_sr_read. Env var documented in docs/internal/BOOT.md (parent repo).

Workspace-local patch; never upstreamed (per sdl_ai_policy memory +
vendor/SDL/CLAUDE.md notice).
